%% Every construct this package styles, in one document. It is the coverage
%% gate's input: a construct missing from here is a construct the gate cannot
%% check, so add to this file whenever the language grows one.

# A heading

Prose with /emphasis/, *strong*, `code`, a [link](https://example.com), an
@mention, a #tag, a footnote[^note], {+inserted+}, {-deleted-} and
{#an editorial comment#}.

[^note]: The note's text.

## Admonitions

::: note "With a title"
Body.
:::

::: warning
Without a title.
:::

::: danger "Danger"
Body.
:::

::: tip "Tip"
Body.
:::

::: important "Important"
Body.
:::

## Quotes and figures

> A quoted line.
^ The attribution

::: figure
![alt text](image.png)
^ The caption
:::

![An uncaptioned block image](wide-image.png)

## Tables

|= Column |= Another |
| cell | cell |

## Lists

- [ ] an open task
- [x] a done task

## Code

``` js
const a = 1; // <1>
```

<1> A callout bound to the marker above.

::: code-group
``` js [one.js]
a
```
``` php [two.php]
b
```
:::

## Tabs

::: tabs
::: tab "First"
first panel
:::
::: tab "Second"
second panel
:::
:::

## Disclosure

Ending: :spoiler[the butler did it] and then the credits roll.

::: spoiler "Hidden"
Revealed.
:::

## Math

$$`E = mc^2`

## Reference apparatus

::: glossary
API
:  Application Programming Interface
:::

An :index[indexed term] in prose.

::: toc
:::

::: list-table
- - row one, cell one
  - row one, cell two
- - row two, cell one
  - row two, cell two
:::

## Diagrams

%% Every diagram renderer the stylesheet has rules for. The spec corpus carries
%% no diagram fence at all, so without these the rules for .mermaid, .d2 and
%% the rest are checked against nothing.

```mermaid
graph TD; a-->b;
```

```d2
a -> b
```

```plantuml
a -> b
```

```dot
digraph { a -> b }
```

```wavedrom
{ "signal": [] }
```

```abc
X:1
```

```vega-lite
{ "mark": "bar" }
```

```chart
{ "type": "bar" }
```

## Diff presentation

{.diff}
```js
+added
-removed
```

## Line breaks

::: |
a line
another line
:::

::: \
one
two
:::

